From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TheDBP <TheDBP@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 22:03:45 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] ether: volume panel by the keys

Put the volume panel on the left, where this device's volume keys are, and raise it to meet them.
The rocker sits at about 34% of screen height rather than the middle. -180dp was the first fit, from a
homography onto a photo of the device; -150dp is the measured correction, taken from a photo with the
panel and the keys in the same frame, which removes the fit error.

def_volume_panel_on_left is a first-boot default only; Settings > System > Buttons still wins for
anyone who changes it.
---
 .../base/packages/SystemUI/res/values/dimens.xml   | 14 ++++++++++++++
 .../res/values/defaults.xml                        |  7 +++++++
 2 files changed, 21 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 overlay/frameworks/base/packages/SystemUI/res/values/dimens.xml
 create mode 100644 overlay/lineage-sdk/packages/LineageSettingsProvider/res/values/defaults.xml

diff --git a/overlay/frameworks/base/packages/SystemUI/res/values/dimens.xml b/overlay/frameworks/base/packages/SystemUI/res/values/dimens.xml
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..89a616c
--- /dev/null
+++ b/overlay/frameworks/base/packages/SystemUI/res/values/dimens.xml
@@ -0,0 +1,14 @@
+<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
+<resources>
+    <!-- The Robin's volume rocker is at roughly 31% of the screen's height, not the middle, so the
+         stock centred panel sits well below the keys being pressed. Measured by fitting a
+         homography from a photo of the device to screen coordinates using four on-screen landmarks:
+         the two buttons come out at y 505 and y 694 of 1920, midpoint 600. The panel's own centre
+         is 961 (it spans 607..1315).
+
+         -180dp was the first fit and overshot. Re-measured against a photo of the panel and the
+         keys in the same frame, which is a far better comparison than fitting the keys alone: the
+         panel came out 65 photo-px high against a panel height of 795 photo-px for 708 device px,
+         so 58 device px = 29dp too far. The keys are at device y 659, about 34% of the screen. -->
+    <dimen name="volume_dialog_offset_y">-150dp</dimen>
+</resources>
diff --git a/overlay/lineage-sdk/packages/LineageSettingsProvider/res/values/defaults.xml b/overlay/lineage-sdk/packages/LineageSettingsProvider/res/values/defaults.xml
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..65e87f3
--- /dev/null
+++ b/overlay/lineage-sdk/packages/LineageSettingsProvider/res/values/defaults.xml
@@ -0,0 +1,7 @@
+<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
+<resources>
+    <!-- The volume keys are on the Robin's left edge, so put the panel on the same side. This is a
+         first-boot default only: it seeds the settings database when it is created, and anyone who
+         changes it under Settings > System > Buttons > "Show panel on left" keeps their choice. -->
+    <bool name="def_volume_panel_on_left">true</bool>
+</resources>
